## ISS-004: No rate limiting on web-admin login endpoint

### File
`/root/Redball/web-admin/server.js`

### Original (top imports)
```javascript
const express = require('express');
```

### Replacement (top imports)
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
```

### Original (login route registration)
```javascript
// Auth endpoints
app.post('/api/auth/login', async (req, res) => {
```

### Replacement
```javascript
const loginLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  max: 5,
  standardHeaders: true,
  message: { error: 'Too many login attempts, please try again later.' }
});

// Auth endpoints
app.post('/api/auth/login', loginLimiter, async (req, res) => {
```

### Also update
`/root/Redball/web-admin/package.json` dependencies to add `"express-rate-limit": "^8.3.2"`, then run `npm install`.

### Reason
Prevents online brute-force attacks against the single admin account by limiting login attempts per IP.

### Verification
`npm install` + `npm test` + simulate rapid `/api/auth/login` requests and verify 429 responses after the limit.
